    description:
      "The reason you did not post this week is usually not lost passion or a dry idea list, it is that you are waiting to feel like making something before you make it, treating the absent urge as an honest signal (the timing is off, the spark is gone) when it is only the ordinary state of not having started yet and was never going to lift on its own from the couch. The belief underneath is that motivation comes first and action second, but for creative work the order is usually backwards, which shows up most clearly in the strongest treatment for people who cannot make themselves do anything, behavioral activation, built on the plain finding that action comes before motivation not after (you do the thing without the feeling and the wanting arrives during, dragged along by having started, which is why the hardest part of making anything is the sixty seconds before you begin and the resistance is gone two minutes in). Where that drive comes from backs it up: Amabile and Kramer&apos;s close to 12,000 daily diary entries from 238 people found the biggest lift to motivation on a working day was not praise or reward but making progress on something that mattered, even a small step, so the wanting is an output of the work and not a ticket you need before starting. This is why a gap feeds itself, because the pull to make tracks how recently you last made, so a quiet stretch drains it further and gets misread as lost passion when the truth is you stopped and stopping took the feeling with it, and the creators who look tireless never let the gap widen enough to go cold. The fix is to make one bad-and-finished thing today before you feel like it, small enough that not feeling like it stops being an excuse, because starting is the only known way to produce the state you were waiting to be handed. Distinct from consistency-is-a-systems-problem (design a low-friction loop so a tired you shows up), nothing-you-post-pays-you-back-right-away (the external reward arrives late and starves the habit), you-were-one-purchase-away-from-starting (gear as a purchasable precondition), and you-are-waiting-to-be-qualified (expertise as a precondition): this is about the internal precondition, waiting to feel like it, and how motivation is manufactured by starting rather than required before it.",
